.TH CWE-494 7 "2026-11-15" "CWE Top 25 (2025)" "Software Weakness Reference"
.SH NAME
CWE\-494 \- Download of Code Without Integrity Check
.SH RANK
KEV\-referenced weakness. Not part of the 2025 CWE Top 25; documented here because it appears in the CISA KEV catalog.
.SH CLASSIFICATION
Class: KEV\-referenced weakness.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The product downloads source code or an executable from a remote location and executes the code without sufficiently verifying the origin and integrity of the code. An attacker can execute malicious code by compromising the host server, performing DNS spoofing, or modifying the code in transit.
.SH KNOWN EXPLOITED VULNERABILITIES
CISA KEV catalog (as of 2026-11-15): \fB4\fR exploited CVEs mapped to this weakness. Each entry has the catalog write\-up of how it was used in the wild (not a runnable exploit) and the required remediation. Code\-level vulnerable\->fixed pairs, when curated, are under \fBEXAMPLES\fR.
.SS CVE\-2021\-44168
Fortinet FortiOS, added 2021\-12\-10.
.PP
Fortinet FortiOS Arbitrary File Download.
.PP
\fIHow it is exploited (CISA):\fR
Fortinet FortiOS "execute restore src\-vis" downloads code without integrity checking, allowing an attacker to arbitrarily download files.
.PP
\fIRemediation:\fR
Apply updates per vendor instructions.
 Due 2021\-12\-24.
.PP
